## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Added `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` as a dependency
- Used pnpm package manager as specified in package.json
- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with new dependencies

**2. Configuration** 
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate the Analytics component
- Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next` (Next.js App Router specific import)
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the children
- Preserved all existing code structure, imports, and functionality

**Files Modified:**
- `web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `web/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated lock file with new package dependencies
- `web/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router:

1. Installed the package using `pnpm add @vercel/analytics`
2. Imported the Analytics component from the Next.js-specific export path
3. Placed the component at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with page rendering
4. Maintained the existing code structure including the theme script and all metadata

### Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
- ✓ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✓ ESLint linting passed with no warnings
- ✓ Production build completed successfully
- ✓ All 50 unit tests passed

### Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in the Vercel project dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
4. Analytics data will begin collecting after the next deployment and user visits

The implementation is ready for production deployment.
